        <h3>Retail Equities Membership Program</h3>

        <p>Retail Membership Organizations (“RMOs”) that meet the eligibility requirements described below are eligible to participate in the EDGX Retail Membership Program (the “Program”). For such new Members, the Program provides for discounted firm membership fees, logical and physical port fees, market data fees, and provides opportunity to receive enhanced rebates for retail volume for up to 18 months according to the schedule set forth below, subject to the following:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>To be eligible, a new Member must be approved as an RMO and may not have been approved as an EDGX Equities Exchange RMO member within 18 months prior to approval as an RMO. Eligibility for discounts begins in the month that a new membership application is approved. A Member is eligible to enroll in the Program only once.
            </li>

            <li>A new Member that is, or becomes, an “affiliate” of an existing Member, defined as having at least 75% common ownership between the two entities as reflected on each entity’s Form BD, is ineligible to participate in the Program.
            </li>

            <li>A Member will be considered eligible each month if at least 90% of its submitted orders to EDGX Equities that month are Retail Orders.
            </li>

            <li>The Market Data fees that are eligible for the Program are: External Distribution Fees and the Data Consolidation Fee (“Eligible Market Data Fees”). A firm that was a subscriber to any of the Eligible Market Data Fees within the prior 18 months before becoming approved as a new Member is ineligible for the Program’s Market Data fee discounts. Program discounts cannot be combined with any other discounts applicable to Eligible Market Data Fees.
            </li>

            <li>A new Member that is eligible for the Program will be subject to the following discounts:
            </li>
        </ul>

